// Film-droplet split (entrainment) first increment of the distributed
// two-fluid kernel: rate-driven horizontal pipe with wallis slip so the
// gas velocity varies with the holdup, and an entrainment{} block carrying
// the per-cell droplet fraction d of the liquid. The droplet content
// qd = alpha d rides the gas at its velocity (face flux qd vG upwinded on
// the gas direction; the film flux F - qd vG completes the liquid flux F),
// and d relaxes towards the equilibrium entrained fraction
//   E_eq = clamp((vG - vCrit) / vRef, 0, 1)
// with implicit Euler at the exchange time relaxTime = 8 s. The injected
// liquid arrives 10% entrained (entrainedFraction 0.1) against an initial
// uniform d0 = 0.9, so the run exercises the droplet transport front, the
// film <-> droplet exchange in both directions and the steady profile.
// The mixture velocity is the imposed rate vsl + vsg = 0.4 m/s exactly
// (incompressible phases, rate-driven), so the whole trajectory is closed
// form: Godunov transport of alpha on F(a) = us a^2 + (vm - us) a and of
// the gas flux on G(a) = -us a^2 + (us - vm) a + vm, the water cut and the
// droplet content with their own upwind rules, then the relaxation.
// Steady state: alpha* solves F(alpha*) = vsl = 0.15 (0.5598164906), the
// gas velocity vG* = vm + us alpha* = 0.5679449472 sits inside the ramp
// (E_eq* = (vG* - vCrit)/vRef = 0.6132415787), the water cut is flushed to
// the injected 0.25, and the pressure drop is the per-cell Churchill sum
// on the replicated holdup profile. The droplet fraction does NOT settle
// uniformly: the inlet injects 10% entrained liquid while the exchange
// relaxes d towards E_eq, so the steady state is the developing profile
// tests/check_two_fluid.py mode entrained replicates every step cell by
// cell (1e-9) and anchors the last frame on the closed forms: the uniform
// steady holdup alpha* (root of F(alpha*) = vsl), the flushed water cut,
// the per-cell Churchill pressure drop, and the steady droplet-fraction
// PROFILE - the injected liquid arrives 10% entrained while the exchange
// relaxes d towards E_eq, so the fixed point is the linear recursion
//   d_i = (vG* d_{i-1} + (dx/tau) E_eq*) / (vG* + dx/tau)
// fed by d_0 = (E_in vsl + alpha* (dx/tau) E_eq*) / (alpha* (vG* + dx/tau)):
// entrainment develops along the pipe from ~0.149 at the inlet towards
// E_eq* = 0.6132 downstream (an OLGA-style developing entrainment profile).
fluid
{
    rhoL 1000;
    rhoG 20;
    muL  0.01;
    muG  1e-5;
}

closure
{
    model wallis;
    slipVelocity 0.3;
}

initial
{
    alpha 0.5;
    water 0.8;
}

entrainment
{
    vCrit 0.2;
    vRef 0.6;
    relaxTime 8;
    initial 0.9;
}

pipe
{
    length 20;
    diameter 0.02;
    roughness 0;
    angleDeg 0;
    sections 20;
}

boundaries
{
    inlet  { type phaseRates; vsl 0.15; vsg 0.25; waterFraction 0.25;
             entrainedFraction 0.1; }
    outlet { type fixedPressure; p 0; alpha 0.5; waterFraction 0.5;
             entrainedFraction 0.5; }
}

time
{
    dt 0.1;
    endTime 400;
    reportEvery 100;
}
